WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.660
- Hey guys, welcome to another episode

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.060
of the Wednesday Checkup.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.120
Before we get to the topic
at hand, which is COVID-19,

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.760
we have to address the
protest currently going

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.620
on, and the murder of George
Floyd at the hands of police.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:17.200
I wholeheartedly, with every
ounce of my being, denounce

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.270
and condemn racism of any kind,

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.590
especially to those of the black community

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:23.280
at the hands of police.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.740
Racism isn't just a human rights issue.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.450
It's also a health issue.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:31.440
Your zip code says more
about how long you'll live

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.620
and the quality of life you'll live more

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.150
than your cholesterol score.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:37.570
And that's a huge problem in our nation,

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.080
and it needs to be addressed.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.430
Know that I stand in firm support,

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.350
in solidarity, with
those who are protesting

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.130
these racial injustices.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.900
In fact, I heard a really great speech

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.240
the other day by Killer Mike,

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.540
and I'm gonna be linking
it to my end card.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.670
Check it out for sure.
at the end of this video.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.580
Speaking of video, I once again have

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.190
to point out that I'm disappointed
in our nation's media.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:02.100
At a time where we need unity,

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.240
they're sowing seeds of divisiveness.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.730
They're only highlighting

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.594
the protests when they get violent.

00:01:07.594 --> 00:01:10.240
They're not showing the
countless individuals

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.060
that are out there, they are protecting

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.070
themselves by socially distancing,

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:17.750
wearing masks, being
responsible and being peaceful.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.690
There are plenty of these examples,

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:23.410
but they are far and fewer
between on our media channels.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:24.510
And that's a problem.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.290
We need to be able to trust the media

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:29.190
to tell us the truth so that
we can make better decisions

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:30.960
for ourselves and our families.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.743
To sum up my message, Black lives matter.

00:01:35.806 --> 00:01:38.480
(casual inspiring music)

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.610
And speaking of Black lives mattering,

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:44.710
something that has given me concern, worry

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.930
about black lives is the fact that

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:50.220
so many Black communities are out there

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:53.980
protesting because they have
to at a time of a pandemic

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.190
where they're not only putting
their lives on the line

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.500
because of police injustice,

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.750
but also because of this virus.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.890
And COVID-19 has already dramatically

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.960
and drastically affected
communities of color

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.900
disproportionately in
comparison to other communities.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.700
So I worry and I hope that the masks,

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.040
the social distancing measures,

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.090
the hand washing is going to be enough

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:17.610
to protect these communities.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.720
If you choose to go out and protest,

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.480
please do your best to do it safely.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.710
And if you have someone living with you,

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:27.740
that's a potentially a
high risk COVID-19 patient,

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.680
someone who's over the age of 60,

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.680
has an immunocompromised state,

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.090
or has several other medical conditions,

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.660
do your best to limit your
interaction with that person

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.110
to keep them safe as well.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:39.680
Let's continue this conversation

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.580
about COVID-19 because
people are still getting

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:43.550
sick with it.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:44.960
And at the same time,

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.390
we need to begin the reopening

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.020
of America because the harms

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.180
of staying closed are starting

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.450
to creep up and the benefits

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:51.960
are starting to get limited.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.220
Plus I'm sure we all wanna

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.150
get outdoors as the weather improves,

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:58.120
but we have to do the
going outside and reopening

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.600
of America, strategically and smartly,

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.540
so we don't have another outbreak.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.260
So we don't have this giant second

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.690
wave where thousands die and the hospital

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.170
system potentially breaks.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.730
Those are things we do not want.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.010
So I thought during this video,

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.600
I can answer some of your
most common questions

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.400
about COVID-19 this summer.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.530
What about pools?

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:19.010
My quick answer to that
is you could absolutely

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:21.700
get COVID-19 while being at a pool.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.890
What you can't have
happen is to get COVID-19

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.800
from the actual pool water.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.770
That is if it's properly maintained.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:31.820
If the pool has proper chlorine
levels, bromine levels,

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:35.340
the CDC has stated that
there cannot be transmission

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:38.070
of COVID-19 from the actual pool water.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.490
But that doesn't mean if Bobby or Sally

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.560
is right in front of you

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:43.440
and they're coughing and
sneezing the virus all over

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:44.770
you, that you can't get sick.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:45.890
You still can.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:48.400
So all those other rules still apply.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.430
Covering your face when
you're out of the water,

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:51.810
washing your hands frequently,

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.650
especially after you
touch ladders, doorknobs,

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.550
and all the other public surfaces.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.680
And finally, keeping six
feet away from others

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.210
in or out of the water.

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:02.560
What about the beach?

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.250
Everyone wants to go to the beach.

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:07.200
And I think the first thing
you have to do is check local

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.810
and state restrictions.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.290
Every beach has different rules,

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.350
and that's because different areas

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.580
are in different stages of this pandemic.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.590
Certain areas have already seen their peak

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:17.790
and are dropping down.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.080
Other areas are hitting all time highs.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:22.240
So those two beaches
will have different rules

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.830
and different implications.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.670
The one thing that works for everybody

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:27.137
is six feet away from others,

00:04:27.137 --> 00:04:29.860
no matter if you're swimming or on land,

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:31.410
making sure your face is covered

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:32.780
when you're out of the water.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.240
Please don't get your masks wet,

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.210
cause if you do, they become useless

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.900
and they actually cause other problems.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:39.130
And actually a good recommendation

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:40.980
here would be potentially
to bring two masks

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.640
with you, or two face coverings.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.330
And finally, remembering to
wash your hands frequently.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.200
As a side note, don't forget your SPF.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.620
I actually received a lot of
questions from my patients

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.860
about whether or not the
sun will actually kill

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:54.450
the virus on the beach.

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:57.210
And, there is some sliver of truth

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:59.560
to this, meaning that the virus does live

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.540
a shorter period outdoors,

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.290
where the sun's UV rays are there,

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:05.180
but it's not a natural disinfectant

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.840
to the degree where if someone sneezes,

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.320
it automatically gets killed.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.740
It's not that strong.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.590
It just a shorter lifespan,

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:13.190
not a complete elimination.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.710
What about vacations?

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:15.960
Well, first things first,

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.360
if you or someone in your
family member that's gonna

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.500
be traveling is considered high risk,

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.070
over the age of 60,

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.950
have an immunocompromised state,

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.860
have several medical conditions.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:29.440
I think travel is an
unnecessary risk at this time.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.780
That being said, you could
have high-risk travel

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:32.860
and low risk travel.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.050
And to me, if I'm gonna make

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.450
a recommendation to you as a doctor,

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:37.230
I'm gonna recommend low risk travel.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.300
Try going camping in a
remote area, rent a home

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:41.870
instead of staying in a hotel.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:44.010
If you're gonna stay in a
hotel, stay on the first floor

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.660
so you don't need to be in an elevator

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.020
with a group of people,
or maybe potentially

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.900
take the stairs if you are
in a hotel on a higher floor.

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:53.340
Remember, the biggest
risks to your health,

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.130
it's exposure to lots of people

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.520
for a significant period of time.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.510
If you can lower the amount
of people you're running

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:01.560
into, and spend less time with them,

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.050
you're gonna decrease the risk

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.680
that you're facing with COVID-19.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:07.290
At the same time, if
you're otherwise healthy

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:08.410
and you're following all

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:10.850
protocols, covering your
face, washing your hands,

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.090
keeping six feet away from
others when applicable,

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.709
and you get sick with COVID-19,

00:06:14.709 --> 00:06:18.240
90 to 95% of people will be okay.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:20.410
I don't want you to worry about this

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:21.920
where it's going to cause you anxiety.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.600
Remember my motto from the
beginning of this pandemic,

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:26.300
stay alert, not anxious.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:27.400
What about restaurants?

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.090
If you see your local
restaurants beginning to open up,

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.230
do not be afraid to call ahead,

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:34.600
or once you get there, to
ask them what they're going

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:37.800
to be doing to keep you
and your family safe.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.050
If they're not comfortable
answering that question,

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:42.800
feel free to move on and go
to another establishment.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.260
Just like restaurants are
required to answer your questions

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:46.740
about food allergies, they should

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:49.780
be comfortable discussing
COVID-19 safety practices.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:51.120
What about salons?

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:53.260
Well, again, everyone decides what risk

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.339
is okay for them.

00:06:54.339 --> 00:06:57.660
But I will say, if you're
going for a hair color

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:01.440
versus a haircut, I would
consider the hair color

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.080
a riskier procedure.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.700
Not because of its inherent nature

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:05.590
of what they're doing,

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:06.730
but simply because it takes

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.350
a longer period of time,

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:10.500
so you're increasing your exposure

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.530
to potentially sick individuals.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:13.830
We don't know who's sick.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.190
Remember there's a lot of people walking

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:16.560
around who look just fine,

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:18.240
have no symptoms and could potentially

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.450
be spreading this virus.

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:20.710
What about theme parks?

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.080
Well all the regular rules,

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.730
six feet, masks, hand sanitizer,
all of that still applies,

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:27.340
but a piece of advice for theme parks

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.440
is to avoid crowded areas.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.000
If there's a long line somewhere,

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.430
if there's a big group of people,

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.740
try and stay away from that area.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.730
Those are the areas where
the virus spreads quickly.

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:40.700
Remember that COVID-19 spreads
two to three times more

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.490
rapidly than influenza.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:43.550
The last question,

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:45.290
and probably the most important questions

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.890
that folks have been asking me is,

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:50.530
where will America stand
at the end of summer?

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:53.350
And I think the answer of that
question relies heavily on

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:55.110
you and me.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:57.900
There's really a level of
personal responsibility here.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:01.540
If we open America
strategically and smartly,

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.160
and continue monitoring
our hospital systems

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:05.560
and follow all the guidelines

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.810
that we've been talking
about, six foot rule,

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:10.210
wearing masks, washing
our hands frequently,

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:12.450
we can be in a really
good place this summer

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:14.540
to prepare for the fall flu season.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:17.350
But if we don't and we do
everything haphazardly,

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:19.340
we could potentially see another spike

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:22.760
that can cost us thousands
of lives unnecessarily.

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:24.447
FYI, I'm going to be donating all

00:08:24.447 --> 00:08:26.412
of the AdSense revenue and matching

00:08:26.412 --> 00:08:28.710
it to the Southern Poverty Law Center.

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:31.160
So share this video with
your friends and family,

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:33.280
as these COVID-19 tips can potentially

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:34.380
save someone's life.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:37.080
And definitely check out this educational,

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:40.430
moving, motivational speech
by Killer Mike right here,

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:43.804
click it, and as always,
stay happy and healthy.

00:08:43.804 --> 00:08:47.221
(casual inspiring music)

